{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-14T04:35:27.736Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9d7f970542d8df5a0a6bdb3b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","lineage:pm-gh1713","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1713+pm-gh1719","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1713","claim:pm-gh1719","lineage:pm-gh1713","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-o74zyh"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The documented pm get --json to pm update --stdin-json round trip refuses system-maintained metadata: a claimed item's claim_principal and any format-bumped item's pm_format_version are rejected as core fields"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while implementing pm-gh1713 (2026-11-14). docs/COMMANDS.md promises a lossless get, edit, update round trip through --stdin-json. The document adapter in src/sdk/structured-mutations.ts skips a short list of read-only keys (created_at, updated_at, author, collection_counts and similar) and turns every key outside CORE_ITEM_FIELD_KEYS into an extension --field assignment. System-maintained metadata is in neither list, so the round trip fails with core_item_field_requires_dedicated_flag for: claim_principal, present on every item a detected agent harness claimed (reproduced on 2026.11.13: pm claim, pm get --json, pm update --stdin-json); pm_format_version, present on every item with linked-test editor stamps (format 2) or setup entries (format 3); test_runs, the recorded linked-test run summaries. pm-gh1713 adds deferred_fields, which an imported item carries until it is curated, so the defect would hit every mirrored item. Expected: system-maintained keys are read-only in the document adapter, exactly like updated_at and author, and a create document's deferred_fields maps to the create deferral options so a strict tracker can recreate it. Duplicate check: searched stdin-json round trip claim_principal pm_format_version core item field requires dedicated flag; pm-stdin-schema-fields (closed) covered schema and extension fields only."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","area:sdk","round-trip","stdin-json"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-14T04:35:27.736Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-14T04:35:27.736Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm get --json piped into pm update --stdin-json succeeds for a claimed item, a format-2 or format-3 item and an item with deferred fields, without changing claim_principal, pm_format_version or test_runs; A create document carrying deferred_fields recreates the deferral (fields and reason) instead of refusing; A spec reproduces each refusal and proves the round trip"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Piping pm get --json into pm update --stdin-json is lossless for every stored item"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The round trip refuses any item that carries claim_principal, pm_format_version or test_runs"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-gh1713","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-14T04:35:27.736Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-stdin-schema-fields","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-14T04:35:27.736Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"2859d137f450f9e833984cf301a172d779f0ee62e57ba282d4ba795364c8ed3f","item_hash_version":3,"message":"File stdin-json round-trip refusal of system-maintained metadata","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"7a7e281d99195cb2263cbb455793487ed3050ae0458cf7b5743921589d805006"}
